# G8 (graphics): the horizontal scroll bar. A page with half-inch margins is wider than the screen gives it, so the bar has a thumb:
# the arrows, the arrow held (it repeats after a delay and stops on release), the track, the thumb dragged, Shift and the wheel, the
# caret scrolled into view by End, and a click that leaves the view where it is. Every frame's CRC-32 must equal the host's.
@copy wide.rtf
@open WIDE.RTF
@click 616 452          # the right arrow: sixteen pixels
@click 616 452
@down 616 452           # held: nothing until the delay
@wait 3
@wait 6                 # the first repeat, then one a tick
@wait 4
@up 616 452             # released: it stops
@wait 20
@click 8 452            # the left arrow
@click 400 452          # the track right of the thumb: a page
@drag 300 452 40 452    # the thumb dragged back to the left
@shiftwheel 1           # three arrow steps
@wheel 1                # the wheel alone is the page's
@click 300 300          # a click in the page does not scroll
home end                # the caret at the end of the line is scrolled into view
@click 100 120
f10 end enter
